{"statement": "Autonomous weapons systems are commercial hardware built by defense contractors and procured by state militaries, not autonomous historical forces. Software engineers at firms like Palantir or Anduril write the targeting algorithms, and military procurement officers in the Pentagon sign the acquisition contracts. These systems process sensor data to recommend kinetic strikes, but they do not possess legal standing or moral agency. When an algorithm misclassifies a civilian group as combatants, the machine pays no penalty and faces no court martial. The manufacturer profits from the sale, the military command adopts the efficiency metric, and civilian victims bear the lethal cost.

